  "id": "analogue-study",
  "term": "analogue study",
  "definition": "An analogue study is a research design that examines a psychological question in a simulated or imagined version of a real-life situation rather than in the actual setting. In this example, healthy young adults were asked to imagine having an incurable illness so researchers could study likely end-of-life communication.",
